Akture is a lightweight X11 display manager written for AutumnBSD.

A small master runs as root, starts the X server and sessions and is
the only part that talks to PAM.  The login screen runs as an
unprivileged user, draws with pixman and FreeType into shared memory,
and reads the keyboard with libxkbcommon.  The messages between the
two, the state machine of the master and its parsers are verified with
Frama-C and TLA+.

To use it, set akture=YES in /etc/rc.conf.  The login screen needs the
fonts Outfit and Zen Kaku Gothic New in share/akture/fonts, or others
set with font_ui and font_clock in akture.conf.
